PARITY MAP (web → native, per the web source read end-to-end)
  • web hand-rolled popover (manual click-outside + Escape)   → SwiftUI `.popover` (native dismissal,
                                                                 keyboard, anchored presentation, a11y;
                                                                 keeps the two-step "pick scope, then
                                                                 pick format" flow open like the web)
  • web `<Button variant=ghost icon=Download>Export</Button>` → ListExportMenuTrigger (native Button,
                                                                 text-secondary tokens, icon+caption;
                                                                 ChartExportMenu's sibling treatment)
  • web `<button role=menuitem>` CSV/JSON rows               → ListExportFormatRow (tablecells / curlybraces)
  • web scope radios (Visible / Selected fieldset)           → scope section + ListExportScopeRadioRow
  • web `disabled` ("while loading or empty")                → ListExportAvailability ready/loading/empty
                                                                 (loading=spinner, empty=dim; both label
                                                                 "No data to export")
  • web `selectedCount>0` gates the scope fieldset           → ListExportMenuLogic.showsScopeChooser
  • web initial scope = selectedCount>0 ? selected : visible → ListExportMenuLogic.initialScope
  • web effect: selected→visible when selection empties      → ListExportMenuLogic.correctedScope
  • web "export always covers visible when chooser hidden"   → ListExportMenuLogic.effectiveScope
  • web `visibleCount!=null ? "Visible ({{count}})":"Visible"`→ Strings.visibleScopeLabel ({{count}} ungrouped)
  • web `onExportCsv(scope)` / `onExportJson(scope)`         → model.export(format, effectiveScope)
  • web `useTranslation` t(key, default)                     → ListExportMenuStrings facade (P1/S10)
  • web (no view.opened)                                      → ListExportMenuModel.markAppeared (P1/S11)

STATES (every one renders — the trigger is never hidden):
  ready (opens popover w/ optional scope chooser + CSV/JSON), loading (disabled trigger + spinner),
  empty (dimmed disabled trigger, "No data to export"), and the open-popover with/without scope chooser.
  The web control is purely presentational (its only hook is `useTranslation`; no query), so there is
  NO data-fetch axis — no stale/offline/error/retry chrome is fabricated (that would be invented
  behaviour / silent drift, covenant #2/#9). The loading + empty reasons are the native split of the
  single web `disabled` boolean, which the web prop documents as set "while data is loading or empty".

